WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.549
Welcome to our training, sales manipulation and competitor abuse.

00:00:03.549 --> 00:00:05.520
In this video, you'll learn

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.108
what sales manipulation and competitor abuse are, as well as how it occurs.

00:00:10.108 --> 00:00:11.520
You'll also learn about

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:16.204
our seller code of conduct and ways to be responsible with your account when partnering with third-

00:00:16.204 --> 00:00:16.480
party

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.465
service providers.

00:00:17.465 --> 00:00:22.880
Other topics we'll cover include actions taken when policy violations occur,

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.840
how to reinstate your account or resolve a warning, and best practices to help you avoid

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.225
committing policy violations.

00:00:29.225 --> 00:00:33.840
Sales manipulation occurs when sellers hire a third-party service

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.880
provider or use controlled buyer accounts to place orders or generate search traffic against

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.020
their own listing.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:44.960
Competitor abuse occurs when a seller uses a controlled buyer account to damage

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:45.750
another seller.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:51.280
Buyer accounts can be used to tie up another seller's inventory, place fake reviews

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.292
or feedback, or send abusive buyer seller messages.

00:00:54.292 --> 00:00:57.680
The seller code of conduct is a policy that

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:04.320
requires all sellers to act fairly and honestly in the Amazon store to ensure a safe buying and

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.255
selling experience.

00:01:05.255 --> 00:01:10.400
Some examples of seller code of conduct violations include manipulating any

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:16.160
sales by placing orders against your own listings using controlled buyer accounts, compensating

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.635
customers to purchase your products, and creating a super URL to artificially inflate traffic on

00:01:21.635 --> 00:01:22.000
a

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.944
search word or a specific ASIN.

00:01:23.944 --> 00:01:28.480
You also shouldn't allow other people to act on your behalf in a way

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:34.027
that violates Amazon's seller code of conduct policy or your agreement with Amazon.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:34.880
Some other

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:40.800
examples include if a third-party you work with violates Amazon policies on your behalf,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.840
you'll be held accountable whether the violation was conducted with or without your knowledge.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.800
It's your responsibility to ensure the right people have access to your seller central account.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:57.600
Violating the seller code of conduct or any other Amazon policy may result in warnings or

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:03.680
actions against your account, such as cancellation of listings, suspension or forfeiture of payments,

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.455
and removal of selling privileges.

00:02:05.455 --> 00:02:09.360
Make sure to review our selling policies and seller code of

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.863
conduct help page for more information.

00:02:11.863 --> 00:02:15.200
You'll also receive warnings about your policy violations

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.446
under policy compliance on your account health page.

00:02:18.446 --> 00:02:20.880
Click policy violation warnings to learn

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.348
more about a violation.

00:02:22.348 --> 00:02:27.120
When an account is deactivated, you'll receive an alert on your seller central

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.980
page and your account health page stating your account has been deactivated.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.600
To resolve the warnings

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:38.880
on your account, review the warnings on your account health page and then follow the guidance

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.630
in the next steps column.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:44.480
If we don't receive the requested information, the warning will remain

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:49.333
on your account for 180 days from the date when it was first posted.

00:02:49.333 --> 00:02:50.720
To reinstate your account,

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:56.560
click reactivate your account on the main seller central page or click the reactivate your account

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.184
button in the message box on the account health page.

00:03:00.184 --> 00:03:02.720
Let's cover some best practices to consider

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.800
when maintaining your account health dashboard.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.920
Make sure to always check the seller central and

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.770
account health page where you can quickly learn about any enforcements.

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:13.520
Check these pages for all

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:14.693
stores you operate in.

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:18.800
Be careful about working with any third parties that say they want to help

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:19.160
you.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:22.040
Get specific details on how they'll help you.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:25.280
You will be responsible for actions they take on

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.762
your behalf, even if you aren't aware of those actions.

00:03:28.762 --> 00:03:31.200
Check and read any Amazon emails for

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:36.800
important information regarding selling in the Amazon store, our policies, and actions you need

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:37.568
to take.

00:03:37.568 --> 00:03:42.560
Ensure your employees are trained and that you have appropriate account access controls

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:43.326
in place.

00:03:43.326 --> 00:03:47.920
You're responsible for any action conducted through your buyer or seller accounts.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:53.680
In this video, you learned about how sales manipulation and competitor abuse occur,

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:58.720
as well as the seller code of conduct and our policy regarding partnerships with third party

00:03:58.720 --> 00:03:59.552
service providers.

00:03:59.552 --> 00:04:04.128
We also discussed the actions we take when policy violations occur.

00:04:04.128 --> 00:04:04.960
The ways

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:10.720
to reinstate your account or remove a warning when a policy violation occurs, and the best practices

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:14.048
you can take to avoid committing policy violations.

00:04:14.048 --> 00:04:16.960
This concludes our sales manipulation and competitor

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:17.760
abuse training.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:21.360
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
